         {
          ItemBox[
           PaneBox[
            
            StyleBox["\<\"(******************** Product between BrauerList \
objects *********************)\\nBrauerProduct[d1,d2] returns the product of \
diagrams d1 with d2 where d1 and d2 have the head BrauerList.\\nThe option \
ProductConvention allows one to choose its farovite convention for the \
product. It can takes the value Below or Above. \
\\nBrauerProduct[d1,d2,ProductConvention->Below] computes the product by \
placing d1 below d2. \\nBrauerProduct[d1,d2,ProductConvention->Above] \
computes the product by placing d1 above d2. The default value is Below. \
\\nBrauerProduct[d1, d2, d3, ...] returns the product of d1, d2, d3 ... . \
\\nBrauerProduct works for elements of the algebra. \
\\n(*********************** Product between genetors and symbols  \
*********************************)\\nBrauerProduct[d1, d2, d3, ...] also \
outputs the product of d1, d2, d3 ..., where d1, d2, d3 ... have either the \
head Symbol, GeneratorPerm, GeneratorTrace, JucysMurphyS or \
JucysMurphyB.\\nThe product of generators can be reduced using ToReducedWord.\
\"\>", "InformationUsageText",
             StripOnInput->False,
             LineSpacing->{1.5, 1.5, 3.}],
            FrameMargins->{{10, 10}, {8, 10}}],
           BaseStyle->"InformationUsageSubtitleBackground",
