    "(******************** Product between BrauerList objects \
*********************)\nBrauerProduct[d1,d2] returns the product of diagrams \
d1 with d2 where d1 and d2 have the head BrauerList.\nThe option \
ProductConvention allows one to choose its farovite convention for the \
product. It can takes the value Below or Above. \n\
BrauerProduct[d1,d2,ProductConvention->Below] computes the product by placing \
d1 below d2. \nBrauerProduct[d1,d2,ProductConvention->Above] computes the \
product by placing d1 above d2. The default value is Below. \n\
BrauerProduct[d1, d2, d3, ...] returns the product of d1, d2, d3 ... . \n\
BrauerProduct works for elements of the algebra. \n(*********************** \
Product between genetors and symbols  *********************************)\n\
BrauerProduct[d1, d2, d3, ...] also outputs the product of d1, d2, d3 ..., \
where d1, d2, d3 ... have either the head Symbol, GeneratorPerm, \
GeneratorTrace, JucysMurphyS or JucysMurphyB.\nThe product of generators can \
be reduced using ToReducedWord.", "Documentation" -> None, "OwnValues" -> 
    None, "UpValues" -> None, "DownValues" -> 
    Information`InformationValueForm[
     DownValues, BrauerAlgebra`BrauerProduct, {BrauerAlgebra`BrauerProduct[
         PatternTest[
          Pattern[BrauerAlgebra`Private`arg1, 
