parametrizes the \\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(S\\), \\(n\\)]\\) conjugacy class \
in \\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(B\\), \\(n\\)]\\)(\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\
\[Delta]\\), \\(b\\)]\\)). \\nThey correspond to concatenation of particular \
words (bracelets) in a ternary alphabet (1,2,3) where each word have the same \
number of 1 and 2. \\nTwo words are equilavent if they are related by cyclic \
permutations and inversions. A canonical representative is accesible with the \
function ToCanonicalBracelets[bracelets].\\nThe letters 1,2, and 3 represent \
North arcs, South arcs, and Propagating lines respectively.\\nSee for example \
\\!\\(\\*ButtonBox[StyleBox[\\\"[King&Martin&Parker 2016]\\\", \
\\\"SR\\\"],Active->True,BaseStyle->\\\"Link\\\",ButtonData->\\\"http://dx.\
doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1609.01183\\\"]\\)\\!\\(\\*ButtonBox[StyleBox[\\\"[\
Shalile 2013]\\\", \
\\\"SR\\\"],Active->True,BaseStyle->\\\"Link\\\",ButtonData->\\\"http://dx.\
doi.org/10.1007/s10468-011-9294-2\\\"]\\).\"\>", "InformationUsageText",
