\(b\)]\)). \nThey correspond to concatenation of particular words (bracelets) \
in a ternary alphabet (1,2,3) where each word have the same number of 1 and \
2. \nTwo words are equilavent if they are related by cyclic permutations and \
inversions. A canonical representative is accesible with the function \
ToCanonicalBracelets[bracelets].\nThe letters 1,2, and 3 represent North \
arcs, South arcs, and Propagating lines respectively.\nSee for example \
